---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="One Air Fryer to Rule Them All: Ninja Speedi Review" description="It looks like it belongs in an industrial kitchen. But it genuinely replaces several appliances — and that earns it a permanent spot on the counter.">
<style>
  main { max-width: 860px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2.5rem 1.25rem 5rem; }
  .back-link { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.4rem; font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text-muted); text-decoration: none; margin-bottom: 1.75rem; transition: color 0.2s; }
  .back-link:hover { color: var(--rust); }
  .post-meta { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .post-tag { display: inline-block; background: var(--rust); color: white; font-size: 0.65rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.15em; text-transform: uppercase; padding: 0.25rem 0.65rem; border-radius: 2px; }
  .post-date { font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; font-family: 'Fraunces', serif; }
  .post-title { font-family: 'Fraunces', serif; font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 5vw, 2.4rem); font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.15; color: var(--brown); margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
  .post-subtitle { font-family: 'Fraunces', serif; font-size: 1rem; font-style: italic; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 2rem; padding-bottom: 2rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); line-height: 1.6; }
  .product-hero { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 280px 1fr; gap: 2.5rem; align-items: start; background: var(--warm-white); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 2px; padding: 2rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  @media (max-width: 620px) { .product-hero { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .product-hero-image { width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: 2px; display: block; }
  .product-hero-info { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.25rem; }
  .product-name { font-family: 'Fraunces', serif; font-size: 1.4rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--brown); line-height: 1.2; }
  .product-quick-stats { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem; }
  .quick-stat { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 0.6rem; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text); line-height: 1.4; }
  .quick-stat-icon { font-size: 1rem; width: 1.25rem; text-align: center; flex-shrink: 0; margin-top: 0.1rem; }
  .quick-stat strong { color: var(--brown); }
  .buy-btn { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; background: var(--rust); color: white; font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; padding: 0.85rem 1.5rem; border-radius: 2px; text-decoration: none; transition: background 0.2s; }
  .buy-btn:hover { background: #a84825; }
  .affiliate-note { font-size: 0.68rem; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; text-align: center; }
  .post-body { font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text); margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .post-body p { margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .post-body h2 { font-family: 'Fraunces', serif; font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--brown); margin: 2rem 0 0.85rem; padding-bottom: 0.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .feature-list { list-style: none; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.85rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .feature-item { background: var(--warm-white); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 3px solid var(--rust); border-radius: 0 2px 2px 0; padding: 0.9rem 1.25rem; }
  .feature-title { font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--brown); margin-bottom: 0.25rem; }
  .feature-text { font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.55; }
  .downside-box { background: var(--cream); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 3px solid var(--tan); border-radius: 0 2px 2px 0; padding: 1rem 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  .downside-label { font-size: 0.65rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.15em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 0.35rem; }
  .downside-text { font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; line-height: 1.55; }
  .verdict { background: var(--warm-white); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 2px; padding: 1.75rem 2rem; }
  .verdict-label { font-size: 0.68rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.18em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--rust); margin-bottom: 1.1rem; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.6rem; }
  .verdict-label::after { content: ''; flex: 1; height: 1px; background: var(--border); }
  .rating-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(140px, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
  .rating-item { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.3rem; }
  .rating-label { font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .rating-stars { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.15rem; }
  .star { font-size: 1rem; color: var(--tan); line-height: 1; }
  .star.full { color: var(--rust); }
  .star.half { position: relative; color: var(--tan); }
  .star.half::before { content: '★'; position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; width: 50%; overflow: hidden; color: var(--rust); }
  .rating-score { font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--brown); margin-left: 0.3rem; }
  .rating-final { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.75rem; padding-top: 1rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
  .rating-final-label { font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--brown); }
  .rating-final-score { font-family: 'Fraunces', serif; font-size: 1.3rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--rust); }
  .verdict-text { font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; line-height: 1.6; font-family: 'Fraunces', serif; }
</style>

<main>
  <a href="/must-haves" class="back-link">← Must-Haves</a>

  <div class="post-meta">
    <span class="post-tag">Must-Have · Kitchen</span>
    <span class="post-date">May 2026 · by Tom</span>
  </div>

  <h1 class="post-title">One Air Fryer to Rule Them All: Ninja Speedi Review</h1>
  <p class="post-subtitle">It looks like it belongs in an industrial kitchen. It's a behemoth. But it genuinely replaces several appliances — and that earns it a permanent spot on the counter.</p>

  <div class="product-hero">
    <img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71VqX10FbuL._AC_SL1500_.jpg" alt="Ninja Speedi Rapid Cooker & Air Fryer" class="product-hero-image" />
    <div class="product-hero-info">
      <p class="product-name">Ninja Speedi Rapid Cooker &amp; Air Fryer</p>
      <div class="product-quick-stats">
        <div class="quick-stat"><span class="quick-stat-icon">✅</span><span><strong>12 cooking modes</strong> that actually do different things</span></div>
        <div class="quick-stat"><span class="quick-stat-icon">✅</span><span><strong>Two-level cooking</strong> — two foods at once</span></div>
        <div class="quick-stat"><span class="quick-stat-icon">✅</span><span><strong>Replaces several appliances</strong> — steamer, slow cooker, air fryer &amp; more</span></div>
        <div class="quick-stat"><span class="quick-stat-icon">⚠️</span><span><strong>Real learning curve</strong> — give it time</span></div>
      </div>
      <a href="https://amzn.to/3R2xlNU" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="buy-btn">View on Amazon →</a>
      <p class="affiliate-note">Affiliate link — I earn a small commission at no cost to you. Not always expensive — grab it when it goes on sale.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="post-body">
    <p>Unlike a standard air fryer with a pull-out basket, the Ninja Speedi opens from the top — you flip up a hatch like you're climbing out of a tank. Inside is a large crisper plate that sits at two adjustable heights, which means you can cook multiple things at once. Rice on the bottom, chicken up top. One machine, one cook time.</p>
    <p>It has 12 cooking modes, and they actually do different things. This isn't like the "Sport" button on your car that just makes the gas pedal more sensitive — these modes genuinely change how the machine operates.</p>
    <h2>What It Can Do</h2>
  </div>

  <ul class="feature-list">
    <li class="feature-item">
      <p class="feature-title">Steam, Sear, Bake, Slow Cook &amp; More</p>
      <p class="feature-text">12 modes that actually behave differently. You're not just getting an air fryer — you're replacing a steamer, a slow cooker, and more in one footprint.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="feature-item">
      <p class="feature-title">Two-Level Cooking</p>
      <p class="feature-text">The adjustable crisper plate lets you run two things simultaneously. It's one of those features that sounds like a gimmick until you're cooking a full meal in one shot.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="feature-item">
      <p class="feature-title">Speedi Meals Mode</p>
      <p class="feature-text">The headline feature — supposedly cooks a full meal from scratch in 15 minutes using steam and air fry together. Honestly, I haven't pushed this one enough yet. That's on me. I'll report back.</p>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <div class="downside-box">
    <p class="downside-label">The One Downside — Because I'm Honest</p>
    <p class="downside-text">There is a real learning curve. This machine will cook things faster than you expect, and you will absolutely have a moment where you open the hatch and think — what is happening in here? Trust it. You might not know what it's doing, but it knows.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="verdict">
    <p class="verdict-label">Tested By Tom Verdict</p>
    <div class="rating-grid">
      <div class="rating-item"><span class="rating-label">Ease of Use</span><div class="rating-stars"><span class="star full">★</span><span class="star full">★</span><span class="star full">★</span><span class="star full">★</span><span class="star full">★</span><span class="rating-score">5.0</span></div></div>
      <div class="rating-item"><span class="rating-label">Learning Curve</span><div class="rating-stars"><span class="star full">★</span><span class="star full">★</span><span class="star half">★</span><span class="star">★</span><span class="star">★</span><span class="rating-score">2.5</span></div></div>
      <div class="rating-item"><span class="rating-label">Results</span><div class="rating-stars"><span class="star full">★</span><span class="star full">★</span><span class="star full">★</span><span class="star full">★</span><span class="star">★</span><span class="rating-score">4.0</span></div></div>
      <div class="rating-item"><span class="rating-label">Versatility</span><div class="rating-stars"><span class="star full">★</span><span class="star full">★</span><span class="star full">★</span><span class="star full">★</span><span class="star full">★</span><span class="rating-score">5.0</span></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="rating-final">
      <span class="rating-final-label">Final Score</span>
      <span class="rating-final-score">4.13 / 5</span>
      <div class="rating-stars"><span class="star full">★</span><span class="star full">★</span><span class="star full">★</span><span class="star full">★</span><span class="star">★</span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="verdict-text">This thing works great and will replace several appliances. The learning curve is real — it has so many modes that it takes time to figure out what you're doing. But once you do, it's remarkably simple. If you cook for a family and want one machine that can genuinely do it all, this is it.</p>
  </div>

</main>
</Layout>
